    {
      "type": "text", "id": "d5_t", "x": 50, "y": 730, "width": 680, "height": 110,
      "text": "5.  dotnet run --project NextAurora.AppHost\n     App boots → Program.cs hits:  if (app.Environment.IsDevelopment()) await app.Services.MigrateDatabaseAsync<CatalogDbContext>();\n     MigrateDatabaseAsync resolves the context from DI, calls Database.MigrateAsync(ct)\n     → EF reads __EFMigrationsHistory table → finds AddPromotionCodes not applied → runs Up() → INSERT into __EFMigrationsHistory\n     Pending migrations apply in order. Done.",
      "originalText": "5.  dotnet run --project NextAurora.AppHost\n     App boots → Program.cs hits:  if (app.Environment.IsDevelopment()) await app.Services.MigrateDatabaseAsync<CatalogDbContext>();\n     MigrateDatabaseAsync resolves the context from DI, calls Database.MigrateAsync(ct)\n     → EF reads __EFMigrationsHistory table → finds AddPromotionCodes not applied → runs Up() → INSERT into __EFMigrationsHistory\n     Pending migrations apply in order. Done.",
      "fontSize": 11, "fontFamily": 3, "textAlign": "left", "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "strokeColor": "#065f46", "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 1, "strokeStyle": "solid", "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100, "angle": 0,
      "seed": 200029, "version": 1, "versionNonce": 200030,
      "isDeleted": false, "groupIds": [], "boundElements": null, "link": null, "locked": false, "containerId": "d5", "lineHeight": 1.3
    },

    {
      "type": "text", "id": "prod_title", "x": 800, "y": 170, "width": 700, "height": 28,
      "text": "PROD (NOT in-process)",
      "originalText": "PROD (NOT in-process)",
      "fontSize": 18, "fontFamily": 3, "textAlign": "left", "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#b91c1c", "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 1, "strokeStyle": "solid", "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100, "angle": 0,
      "seed": 300001, "version": 1, "versionNonce": 300002,
      "isDeleted": false, "groupIds": [], "boundElements": null, "link": null, "locked": false, "containerId": null, "lineHeight": 1.25
    },

    {
      "type": "rectangle", "id": "prod_problem", "x": 800, "y": 210, "width": 700, "height": 140,
      "strokeColor": "#b91c1c", "backgroundColor": "#fecaca",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 2, "strokeStyle": "solid", "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100, "angle": 0,
      "seed": 300003, "version": 1, "versionNonce": 300004,
      "isDeleted": false, "groupIds": [], "boundElements": [{"id":"prod_problem_t","type":"text"}], "link": null, "locked": false, "roundness": {"type": 3}
    },
    {
      "type": "text", "id": "prod_problem_t", "x": 810, "y": 222, "width": 680, "height": 110,
      "text": "❌  Why NOT in-process at startup:\n\nWith multiple replicas behind a load balancer:\n• replica A starts → calls Migrate → acquires the __EFMigrationsLock → applies migration\n• replicas B, C start at the same time → also call Migrate → BLOCK on the lock,\n  THEN race: one ends up applying the same migration twice / sees the history table in flux\n• Outcome: random startup failures, migration-history corruption, retry storms.\nThe IsDevelopment() gate exists to prevent this.",
      "originalText": "❌  Why NOT in-process at startup:\n\nWith multiple replicas behind a load balancer:\n• replica A starts → calls Migrate → acquires the __EFMigrationsLock → applies migration\n• replicas B, C start at the same time → also call Migrate → BLOCK on the lock,\n  THEN race: one ends up applying the same migration twice / sees the history table in flux\n• Outcome: random startup failures, migration-history corruption, retry storms.\nThe IsDevelopment() gate exists to prevent this.",
      "fontSize": 11, "fontFamily": 3, "textAlign": "left", "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "strokeColor": "#7f1d1d", "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 1, "strokeStyle": "solid", "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100, "angle": 0,
      "seed": 300005, "version": 1, "versionNonce": 300006,
      "isDeleted": false, "groupIds": [], "boundElements": null, "link": null, "locked": false, "containerId": "prod_problem", "lineHeight": 1.3
    },

    {
      "type": "rectangle", "id": "prod_flow", "x": 800, "y": 370, "width": 700, "height": 320,
      "strokeColor": "#047857", "backgroundColor": "#dcfce7",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 2, "strokeStyle": "solid", "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100, "angle": 0,
      "seed": 300007, "version": 1, "versionNonce": 300008,
      "isDeleted": false, "groupIds": [], "boundElements": [{"id":"prod_flow_t","type":"text"}], "link": null, "locked": false, "roundness": {"type": 3}
    },
    {
      "type": "text", "id": "prod_flow_t", "x": 810, "y": 385, "width": 680, "height": 300,
      "text": "✓  Correct prod flow — SEPARATE PRE-DEPLOY STEP:\n\n  1.  CI builds + tests + packages the app image\n\n  2.  CI runs migrations as a one-shot job (NOT inside the app):\n       dotnet ef database update \\\n          --project CatalogService.Infrastructure \\\n          --startup-project CatalogService.Api \\\n          --connection \"$PROD_CATALOG_DB_CONNECTION\"\n      This connects from CI's runner, applies pending migrations, exits.\n      Same EF tooling as dev — just run from a different host.\n\n  3.  CI deploys the new app image to k8s / ECS / wherever.\n      App pods start with NO migration call (the IsDevelopment gate is false in prod).\n\n  4.  Each app replica boots cleanly, schema already up-to-date.\n\nTracked in STATUS.md → \"Production migration deploy step\" (tooling exists; the\nCI step is not yet automated since we don't have a deploy target).",
      "originalText": "✓  Correct prod flow — SEPARATE PRE-DEPLOY STEP:\n\n  1.  CI builds + tests + packages the app image\n\n  2.  CI runs migrations as a one-shot job (NOT inside the app):\n       dotnet ef database update \\\n          --project CatalogService.Infrastructure \\\n          --startup-project CatalogService.Api \\\n          --connection \"$PROD_CATALOG_DB_CONNECTION\"\n      This connects from CI's runner, applies pending migrations, exits.\n      Same EF tooling as dev — just run from a different host.\n\n  3.  CI deploys the new app image to k8s / ECS / wherever.\n      App pods start with NO migration call (the IsDevelopment gate is false in prod).\n\n  4.  Each app replica boots cleanly, schema already up-to-date.\n\nTracked in STATUS.md → \"Production migration deploy step\" (tooling exists; the\nCI step is not yet automated since we don't have a deploy target).",
      "fontSize": 11, "fontFamily": 3, "textAlign": "left", "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "strokeColor": "#065f46", "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 1, "strokeStyle": "solid", "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100, "angle": 0,
      "seed": 300009, "version": 1, "versionNonce": 300010,
      "isDeleted": false, "groupIds": [], "boundElements": null, "link": null, "locked": false, "containerId": "prod_flow", "lineHeight": 1.3
    },

    {
      "type": "rectangle", "id": "immut", "x": 40, "y": 880, "width": 1460, "height": 240,
      "strokeColor": "#b45309", "backgroundColor": "#fef3c7",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 2, "strokeStyle": "dashed", "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100, "angle": 0,
      "seed": 400001, "version": 1, "versionNonce": 400002,
      "isDeleted": false, "groupIds": [], "boundElements": [{"id":"immut_t","type":"text"}], "link": null, "locked": false, "roundness": {"type": 3}
    },
    {
      "type": "text", "id": "immut_t", "x": 60, "y": 895, "width": 1420, "height": 28,
      "text": "⚠  THE IMMUTABLE-ONCE-APPLIED RULE  (CLAUDE.md \"Performance Rules\")",
      "originalText": "⚠  THE IMMUTABLE-ONCE-APPLIED RULE  (CLAUDE.md \"Performance Rules\")",
      "fontSize": 15, "fontFamily": 3, "textAlign": "left", "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#92400e", "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 1, "strokeStyle": "solid", "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100, "angle": 0,
      "seed": 400003, "version": 1, "versionNonce": 400004,
      "isDeleted": false, "groupIds": [], "boundElements": null, "link": null, "locked": false, "containerId": "immut", "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "type": "text", "id": "immut_body", "x": 60, "y": 930, "width": 1420, "height": 180,
      "text": "Once a migration has run anywhere (including dev), it is FROZEN. Never edit it. Why: editing drifts the ModelSnapshot.cs from\nthe history table → next migration generation produces broken output OR (worse) deploying the edited migration to a DB that already\nran the old version either no-ops or corrupts schema.\n\nDestructive changes (drop column / drop table / rename / NOT NULL on existing column) — DO NOT do in one migration:\n\n   Step A:  Deploy code that no longer reads the column.   ← deploy + wait one release cycle\n   Step B:  Wait until all in-flight requests using the old code have completed.\n   Step C:  Generate a new migration that drops the column.  Deploy.\n\nDoing all three in one migration is how production outages happen during deploys: old pods crash on the missing column\nwhile new pods are still rolling out.",
      "originalText": "Once a migration has run anywhere (including dev), it is FROZEN. Never edit it. Why: editing drifts the ModelSnapshot.cs from\nthe history table → next migration generation produces broken output OR (worse) deploying the edited migration to a DB that already\nran the old version either no-ops or corrupts schema.\n\nDestructive changes (drop column / drop table / rename / NOT NULL on existing column) — DO NOT do in one migration:\n\n   Step A:  Deploy code that no longer reads the column.   ← deploy + wait one release cycle\n   Step B:  Wait until all in-flight requests using the old code have completed.\n   Step C:  Generate a new migration that drops the column.  Deploy.\n\nDoing all three in one migration is how production outages happen during deploys: old pods crash on the missing column\nwhile new pods are still rolling out.",
      "fontSize": 11, "fontFamily": 3, "textAlign": "left", "verticalAlign": "top",
      "strokeColor": "#374151", "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 1, "strokeStyle": "solid", "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100, "angle": 0,
      "seed": 400005, "version": 1, "versionNonce": 400006,
      "isDeleted": false, "groupIds": [], "boundElements": null, "link": null, "locked": false, "containerId": null, "lineHeight": 1.3
    },

    {
      "type": "rectangle", "id": "history", "x": 40, "y": 1150, "width": 1460, "height": 130,
      "strokeColor": "#1e293b", "backgroundColor": "#1e293b",
      "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 1, "strokeStyle": "solid", "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100, "angle": 0,
      "seed": 500001, "version": 1, "versionNonce": 500002,
      "isDeleted": false, "groupIds": [], "boundElements": [{"id":"history_t","type":"text"}], "link": null, "locked": false, "roundness": {"type": 3}
    },
    {
      "type": "text", "id": "history_t", "x": 55, "y": 1165, "width": 1440, "height": 110,
      "text": "// What lives in each Infrastructure project's Migrations/ folder (committed to git)\n\n20260503040949_InitialCreate.cs              -- the migration class with Up() + Down() methods\n20260503040949_InitialCreate.Designer.cs     -- snapshot of the model AT this migration (immutable once applied)\nCatalogDbContextModelSnapshot.cs             -- LIVE snapshot of the current model (regenerated each migration add)\n\n// And in the DB:\nCREATE TABLE __EFMigrationsHistory ( MigrationId nvarchar(150) PK, ProductVersion nvarchar(32) );\n-- Each Migrate() call: read this table, find unapplied entries, run their Up(), INSERT into this table.",
      "originalText": "// What lives in each Infrastructure project's Migrations/ folder (committed to git)\n\n20260503040949_InitialCreate.cs              -- the migration class with Up() + Down() methods\n20260503040949_InitialCreate.Designer.cs     -- snapshot of the model AT this migration (immutable once applied)\nCatalogDbContextModelSnapshot.cs             -- LIVE snapshot of the current model (regenerated each migration add)\n\n// And in the DB:\nCREATE TABLE __EFMigrationsHistory ( MigrationId nvarchar(150) PK, ProductVersion nvarchar(32) );\n-- Each Migrate() call: read this table, find unapplied entries, run their Up(), INSERT into this table.",
